tsx src/transfer.ts` prints one line of hex and nothing else. Two runs give byte-identical output, because ED25519 signatures are deterministic.\n- I decoded the output with `Transaction.fromBytes` in a temporary script, which I then deleted:\n  - transaction ID `0.0.1001@1793000000.000000000`\n  - memo `invoice 42`\n  - node `0.0.3`\n  - transfers `0.0.1001: -100000000` and `0.0.1002: +100000000` tinybar\n  - `publicKey.verifyTransaction(tx)` returns `true`\n\nNothing was submitted to any network.\nEOF\nnpx tsc --noEmit && echo ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":25224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3398d58-c2fa-47ef-bff3-86cb618f72c6","uuid":"9a42f20b-ad81-4fd3-8798-eb8c740c70e4","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:10:36.025Z","request_id":"req_011CgtMcDsF9PY3c7TFUQ8zs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01U2pjfRLAhYkfoioEiqiKxC":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-ni5yox && printf 'node_modules/\\n' > .gitignore && cat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# What I did\n\n## 1. Added the Hedera JavaScript SDK\n- Checked npm: the current `latest` version of `@hashgraph/sdk` is **2.81.0** (dist-tags: `latest: 2.81.0`, `beta: 2.81.0-beta.1`).\n- Ran `npm install @hashgraph/sdk@2.81.0`. This added `\"@hashgraph/sdk\": \"^2.81.0\"` to `dependencies` in `package.json` and created `package-lock.json`.\n- npm held back the install scripts for `protobufjs` and `esbuild` (npm's install-script approval feature). I didn't approve them. `tsx`, `tsc` and the SDK all work without them.\n- Added a `.gitignore` containing `node_modules/`.\n\n## 2. Wrote `src/transfer.ts`\nRun it with `npx tsx src/transfer.ts` (or